{
  "title": "The three cases side by side",
  "note": "Nominative = subject (der, ein, er). Accusative = direct object (den, einen, ihn). Dative = indirect object, the receiver (dem, einem, ihm). Pronouns: ich/mich/mir, du/dich/dir, er/ihn/ihm, sie/sie/ihr, wir/uns/uns, Sie/Sie/Ihnen. A dative noun usually comes before an accusative noun: Ich gebe dem Kind den Ball.",
  "src": { "t": "Grimm Grammar: Cases overview and dative pronouns", "u": "https://coerll.utexas.edu/gg/gr/pro_04.html" },
  "items": [
    { "c": "___ Hund schläft. (the, subject)", "a": "Der", "d": ["Den", "Dem"] },
    { "c": "Ich sehe ___ Hund. (the)", "a": "den", "d": ["der", "dem"], "ex": "Ich sehe den Hund.", "exT": "I see the dog." },
    { "c": "Ich gebe ___ Hund Wasser. (the)", "a": "dem", "d": ["den", "der"], "ex": "Ich gebe dem Hund Wasser.", "exT": "I'm giving the dog water." },
    { "c": "Ich wohne bei ___ Freundin. (a)", "a": "einer", "d": ["eine", "einem"] },
    { "c": "Ich besuche ___ Freund. (my)", "a": "meinen", "d": ["meinem", "mein"] },
    { "c": "Ich danke ___ Freund. (my)", "a": "meinem", "d": ["meinen", "mein"] },
    { "c": "Er hilft den ___. (die Männer)", "a": "Männern", "d": ["Männer", "Manns"] },
    { "c": "Siehst du ___? (ich)", "a": "mich", "d": ["mir", "ich"] },
    { "c": "Kannst du ___ helfen? (ich)", "a": "mir", "d": ["mich", "mein"] },
    { "c": "Ich kenne ___. (er)", "a": "ihn", "d": ["ihm", "er"], "ex": "Ich kenne ihn gut.", "exT": "I know him well." },
    { "c": "Ich gebe ___ das Buch. (er)", "a": "ihm", "d": ["ihn", "er"] },
    { "c": "Ich liebe ___. (du)", "a": "dich", "d": ["dir", "du"] },
    { "c": "Wir besuchen ___ morgen. (sie, she)", "a": "sie", "d": ["ihr", "ihnen"] },
    { "c": "Wir danken ___. (sie, she)", "a": "ihr", "d": ["sie", "ihnen"] },
    { "c": "Er ruft ___ an. (wir)", "a": "uns", "d": ["unser", "wir"] },
    { "c": "Ich schreibe ___ eine E-Mail. (Sie)", "a": "Ihnen", "d": ["Sie", "Ihr"] },
    { "c": "___ gehört das Auto? (who)", "a": "Wem", "d": ["Wen", "Wer"], "ex": "Wem gehört das Auto? – Mir.", "exT": "Who does the car belong to? – Me." },
    { "c": "___ siehst du? (who)", "a": "Wen", "d": ["Wem", "Wer"] },
    { "c": "___ kommt heute? (who)", "a": "Wer", "d": ["Wen", "Wem"] },
    { "c": "Ich kaufe Blumen ___ meine Mutter.", "a": "für", "d": ["mit", "von"] },
    { "c": "Wir gehen ___ den Park.", "a": "durch", "d": ["mit", "nach"] },
    { "c": "geben", "a": "to give", "d": ["to take", "to go"], "ex": "Er gibt mir das Geld.", "exT": "He gives me the money." },
    { "c": "schenken", "a": "to give (as a gift)", "d": ["to lend", "to sell"] },
    { "c": "danken", "a": "to thank", "d": ["to think", "to drink"] },
    { "c": "gehören", "a": "to belong to", "d": ["to hear", "to listen to"], "ex": "Das Buch gehört mir.", "exT": "The book belongs to me." },
    { "c": "antworten", "a": "to answer", "d": ["to ask", "to call"] },
    { "c": "zeigen", "a": "to show", "d": ["to draw", "to hide"] },
    { "c": "besuchen", "a": "to visit", "d": ["to look for", "to invite"] },
    { "c": "es gibt", "a": "there is, there are", "d": ["it gives", "it is"], "ex": "Hier gibt es einen Park.", "exT": "There's a park here." },
    { "c": "Er schenkt der Mutter eine Blume.", "a": "He gives the mother a flower.", "d": ["The mother gives him a flower.", "He buys the mother a flower."] }
  ],
  "read": {
    "title": "Das Geschenk",
    "text": [
      "Morgen hat meine Schwester Geburtstag. Sie wird zwanzig. Ich kaufe ihr ein Geschenk.",
      "Zuerst gehe ich mit meinem Bruder in die Stadt. Wir sehen einen schönen Schal. Er ist blau, und Blau ist ihre Lieblingsfarbe. Ich kaufe den Schal für sie.",
      "Mein Bruder schenkt ihr ein Buch. Am Abend geben wir ihr die Geschenke. Sie dankt uns und sagt: \"Der Schal gefällt mir sehr!\""
    ],
    "q": [
      { "q": "Who is having a birthday?", "o": ["The narrator's brother", "The narrator's sister", "The narrator"], "k": 1 },
      { "q": "Why does the narrator choose the scarf?", "o": ["It is cheap", "It is blue, her favorite color", "Her brother likes it"], "k": 1 },
      { "q": "What does the brother give?", "o": ["A book", "A scarf", "Flowers"], "k": 0 }
    ]
  }
}
